Question: Execute a Python Script Directly

Question:
 https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/mepmefz373b4?lecture_hash=t5qc0u6ap8tg

Solution:
echo "#!/usr/bin/env python3" > hello.py
echo "print('Hello from Python')" >> hello.py
chmod 777 hello.py
./hello.py

Approach:
1. we will write the shebang to tell the computer which compiler or interpretor to run the code
2. and ill write the program to be executed
